routing_rules:
- Directory routes topology; it does not govern truth.
- Shared files may appear across multiple model lanes.
- Cross-listing does not transfer authority ownership.
- Governance controls admissibility and claim safety.
- CE-OS defines causal primitives and interaction doctrine.
- Lexicon controls semantic identity and definition stability.
- Gear extracts causal structure rather than validation.
- Prototype remains non-canonical pending validation.
- Navigation artifacts must not become canon.
- Compression must preserve reconstructability.
- Contradictions must remain recoverable rather than hidden.

growth_rule:
note: >
Add new files only when operationally present.
Preserve sparse topology. Avoid speculative directory expansion.
Maintain recoverable authority lanes.

prohibited_directory_behavior:
- validate_claims
- redefine_source_authority
- collapse_contradictions_into_summary
- convert_navigation_into_canon
- erase_unresolved_variables
- replace_governing_files
- silently_mutate_semantic_identity

global_caution:
note: >
Operational validity does not imply causal completeness.
Navigation structure does not replace validation.
Semantic compression remains causally lossy.
Repository authority remains with governing source files.
